\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Secure Department of Freedom Safe House, 24 hours before the Sublime Point assault
\f1\i0 \strokec2 \
Jones reviews his infiltration plans one final time when there's a knock at the door. He draws his weapon immediately\'97no one should know he's here.\
"Agent Jones," says a familiar voice through the door. "We need to talk."\
Jones recognizes the voice with disgust. "Smythe? I thought you were still in the hospital."\
"I've made a remarkable recovery," Haloren Smythe replies. "Are you going to let me in, or shall I continue shouting sensitive information in the hallway?"\
Jones reluctantly opens the door. Haloren Smythe stands before him, looking significantly worse for wear. His left arm is in a sling, his face is still bruised from the wedding reception incident, and he walks with a pronounced limp.\
"How did you find me?"\
Smythe limps past him into the room. "I may have been forcibly retired, but I still have friends in intelligence. I know about your mission to Sublime Point."\
Jones's finger twitches on the trigger of his weapon. "Give me one reason why I shouldn't eliminate you right now."\
"Because I'm going with you," Smythe says calmly. "And because I know things about Gerry Hardman that you don't."\
This gives Jones pause. "What things?"\
Smythe eases himself painfully into a chair. "I've been tracking Hardman for years. Long before you designated him as 'Jihad Man.' His connections go deeper than you realize\'97all the way to CEO Dunhilton himself."\
Jones scoffs. "That's absurd. Dunhilton just ordered me to eliminate Hardman."\
"And doesn't that strike you as convenient?" Smythe asks. "Dunhilton needs a scapegoat for when things go wrong. He's setting you up, Jones."\
"Why should I believe you? You're an Elvi sympathizer."\
Smythe shrugs his good shoulder. "I prefer to think of myself as someone who dislikes being manipulated. Check this." He slides a data crystal across the table.\
Jones reluctantly inserts it into his secure terminal. Photos appear showing Dunhilton and Hardman meeting secretly six months ago. File records indicate massive financial transfers between hidden accounts.\
"They've been working together from the beginning," Smythe explains. "The whole Elvi situation, the TMinus virus, even the wedding reception disaster\'97all orchestrated to create a pretext for taking control of Sublime Point."\
Jones stares at the evidence, his worldview crumbling. "But why? What's at Sublime Point that's worth all this?"\
"That's what we need to find out," Smythe says. "I have an independent insertion method that can get us both in undetected. Once inside, we split up\'97you track Hardman as planned, I gather intelligence on whatever they're really after."\
Jones narrows his eyes. "If you're lying to me\'97"\
"You'll kill me horribly, yes, I'm aware of your limited conversational repertoire." Smythe stands with difficulty. "Now, shall we prepare? The fabric of reality waits for no man, especially not on Christmas Eve."\
As they prepare equipment, Jones finds himself humming "How Great Thou Art" and doesn't immediately stop when he realizes it.}